  "question": {
    "text": "The potential energy of a particle varies as<br />\r<br />\r<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>U</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></math> for <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn></math><br />\r<br />\r&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math> for <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>1</mn></math><br />\r<br />\rFor&nbsp;&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn></math> , the de-Broglie wavelength is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>λ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math>&nbsp; and for <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>1</mn></math>&nbsp; the de-Broglie wavelength is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>λ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>. The total energy of the particle is&nbsp;&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>E</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></math>. Find <math> <mrow> <mfrac> <mrow> <msub> <mi>λ</mi> <mn>1</mn> </msub> </mrow> <mrow> <msub> <mi>λ</mi> <mn>2</mn> </msub> </mrow> </mfrac> </mrow> </math>",
    "image": null
  },
